<title>UK: BADMINTON-SUDIRMAN CUP WORLD TEAM CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BADMINTON-SUDIRMAN CUP WORLD TEAM CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>GLASGOW 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the Sudirman Cup world</p>
<p>team badminton championships on Thursday:</p>
<p>Group 4B</p>
<p>Switzerland  3  Czech Republic  2</p>
<p> Ukraine	3  Wales	     2</p>
<p>Group 7A</p>
<p> Cyprus	 5  Mexico	    0</p>
<p> Malta	  3  Luxembourg	2</p>
<p>Group 7B</p>
<p> Brazil	 5  Argentina	 0</p>
<p> Italy	  4  Slovakia	  1</p>
<p>Group 2A</p>
<p>Germany    3     Taiwan   2</p>
<p>Japan	3     Thailand 2</p>
<p>Group 2B</p>
<p>Malaysia    4	Canada 1</p>
<p>Netherlands 3	Russia 2</p>
<p>Group 4A</p>
<p>Iceland 3		 Bulgaria 2</p>
<p>U.S.    3		 Poland   2</p>
<p>Group 8</p>
<p>Estonia   5	    Chile  0</p>
<p>Lithuania 4	    Greece 1</p>
<p>Group 1A</p>
<p> China     3   South Korea  2</p>
<p>Results (Chinese names first):</p>
<p>Men's singles</p>
<p>Dong Jiong beat Jang Chun-woong 15-9 15-6</p>
<p>Men's doubles</p>
<p>Ge Cheng/Tao Xiaoqiang lost to Kang Kyung-jin/Ha</p>
<p>Tae-kwon 3-15 10-15</p>
<p>Women's singles</p>
<p>Gong Zhichao beat Lee Joo-hyun 11-5 11-0</p>
<p>Women's doubles</p>
<p>Ge Fei/Gu Jun beat Kim Mee-hyang/Kim Shin-young 15-4  15-9</p>
<p>Mixed doubles</p>
<p>Liu Yong/Ge lost to Kim Dong-moon/Ra Kyung-min 15-7 2-15 11-15</p>
<p>Group 3B</p>
<p> India	 4   Norway   1</p>
<p>Group 5 play-offs:</p>
<p> Kazakhstan  4   Belgium  1</p>
<p> Portugal    3   Peru     2</p>
<p>Group 1B</p>
<p>Denmark 3 Indonesia 2</p>
<p>Men's singles</p>
<p>Poul-Erik Hoyer-Larsen beat Heryanto Arbi 17-16 12-15 15-4</p>
<p>Men's doubles Jan Holst-Christensen/Michael Sogaard lost to</p>
<p>R.Subagja and R.Mainaky 15-18 12-15</p>
<p>Women's singles</p>
<p> Camilla Martin lost to Susi Susanti 6-11 3-11     </p>
<p>Women's doubles</p>
<p>R.Olsen/H. Kirkegaard beat Eliza/R.Zelin 17-14 14-17 15-10</p>
<p>Mixed doubles J Erksen/M.Thomsen beat L.Flandy/M.Timur 15-6</p>
<p>15-12</p>
<p>Group 3A</p>
<p>Australia 3 Hong Kong 2 Finland 3 Austria 2</p>
<p>Group 3B</p>
<p>New Zealand 3 Scotland 2</p>
